          %h3#TrivializationsOfThedInvariant Trivializations of the d-invariant
          %p
            When the d-invariant vanishes, then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/e-invariant"} e-invariant
            exists. But in fact, classical constructions of the e-invariant proceed via a
            %em choice of a trivialization
            of the d-invariant and conclude by showing the result to be independent of this choice (this is meant to be brought out at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Adams+e-invariant#ConstructionViaUnitCofiberTheories"} Adams e-invariant – Construction via unit cofiber theories
          %p
            Here we discuss the space of choices of trivializations of the d-invariant (following
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/M-Theory+as+Mf-Theory"} SS 21
          %p
