            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  The two squares on the left are the stabilization of the homotopy pushout squares defining the cofiber space
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_c
                  and the suspension of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mi d
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{n + d - 1}
              %li
                %p
                  The bottom left rectangle (with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Σ
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi e
                          %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^n(e^E)
                  at its top) is the homotopy pushout defining
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi E
                          %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi 𝕊
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^n(E\!/\mathbb{S})
              %li
                %p
                  The classifying map for the given
                  = succeed "-flux," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathcolor => "magenta"}
                          %msup
                            %mi M
                            %mi d
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\color{magenta}M^d}
                  forming the bottom middle square is uniquely implied by the homotopy pushout property of the bottom left square. Moreover, the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
                  implies that this bottom middle square is itself homotopy cartesian.
              %li
                %p
                  The bottom right square is the homotopy pushout defining
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∂
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial
              %li
                %p
                  By the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
                  it follows that also the bottom right rectangle is homotopy cartesian, hence that, after the two squares on the left, it exhibits the third step in the long homotopy cofiber sequence of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Σ
                            %mn ∞
                          %mi c
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^\infty c
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Σ
                            %mrow
                              %mn ∞
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mi c
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^{\infty + 1} c
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∂
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi M
                            %mi d
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ]
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial \big[ M^d \big] = [c]
            %p
              In conclusion, these construction steps yield a map map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                      %mi E
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi M
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^E_{n-1}\!(c) \mapsto M^d
              which is as required.
            %p
